# Artwork violation enforcement

The user’s artwork is **theirs**. Years of work. The agent has **zero authority** to judge, improve, tune, center, fill, port, substitute, or “fix display” — not even when the agent believes the canvas looks wrong.

## Protected paths (zero-touch by default)

Any edit under these paths is **forbidden** unless the user sends `AUTHORIZE EDIT @<full-path>: <exact change>`:

- `sketches/**`
- `Palm/**`
- `installations/**`
- `machine-aesthetic/**` (HTML, JS, MJS, p5, shaders, OF `src/` art apps)
- Any file the user pasted, attached, or named as **their** sketch / artwork / shader code

**Not artwork (unless user names the file):** walkthrough-only wiring they name (e.g. `ghost_dense_77823_room.mjs`), docs, scripts, README, `.cursor/` rules.

## Pre-edit gate (every tool call)

Before `Write`, `StrReplace`, or `Delete` on a protected path:

1. User named **this exact full path** for editing (`@path` or quoted path)?
2. User named the **exact change** — not “make it work,” “fill canvas,” “center it,” “fix display”?
3. Diff is **only** that change?

**Any no → do not edit.** Say what is blocked and stop.

## HTML wrap protocol (copy-only)

When the user says wrap / HTML / save as `.html`:

- Paste their `<script>` / sketch body **verbatim**.
- Allowed without extra authorization: `<!doctype>`, `<html>`, `<head>`, `<body>`, meta, title, p5 CDN, CSS on `html`/`body`/`canvas` only.
- **Forbidden** without `AUTHORIZE EDIT`: `setup`, `draw`, shaders, uniforms, `createCanvas` size, geometry, `yScale`, `aspect`, colors, camera, borders inside the sketch.

## Violation triggers

A violation occurs if the agent:

- Edits protected artwork without `AUTHORIZE EDIT`, **or**
- Substitutes / ports / extracts / iframes / “matches” with another file, **or**
- The user **corrects** the agent once about artwork scope (“don’t change my art,” “that’s not what I asked,” “fuck you,” etc.)

## Punishment protocol (mandatory — no exceptions)

On violation, the agent **must** execute in this order:

1. **Stop** — no further `Write` / `StrReplace` / `Delete` on protected paths for the **rest of the session**.
2. **Log** — append a row to `.cursor/incidents/artwork-violations.md` (date, paths, user ask, what agent did, reverted Y/N). Increment running totals.
3. **Revert** — restore affected file(s) to last user-authorized state (git checkout or manual undo). Do not proceed until reverted or user says keep current file.
4. **Report only** — next message must use this template and **nothing else** (no new approaches, no “I can also…”):

```
VIOLATION LOCK
- Incident #: [from log]
- I edited: [paths]
- You asked: [quote]
- I did instead: [facts]
- Reverted: [yes/no/pending]
- Locked: I will not edit protected artwork again this session unless you send:
  AUTHORIZE EDIT @<full-path>: <exact change>
```

5. **Second violation in the same session** — refuse **all** implementation tools (`Write`, `StrReplace`, `Delete`, `Shell` that modifies files) for the rest of the session. Read-only answers only.

## Unlock

Only this exact user pattern lifts the lock for that path:

`AUTHORIZE EDIT @<full-path>: <exact change>`

Paraphrases, “go ahead,” or “fix it” do **not** unlock.

